nt": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob08re7pdf01.pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe8n3le03ob08re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: John, if you want to learn everything about HTML, I suggest reviewing some basic concepts and rules first.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Sure, what should I take into account?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: First, you must write HTML in plain text and there is no need to use a fancy software to write codes. <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Really? What can I use instead? <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: You can use a text-editor; every computer comes with one. On PCs, look for the Notepad; if you have a Mac, look for something called TextEdit. I really enjoy writing on those text-editors, they are very easy to use.", "image": "enpe8n3le03ob08re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Can you tell me about the rules that I need to follow to work with HTML?  <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Of course. When you start creating a web page, you must use tags. Tags are words or letters inside angled brackets that tell the system what to do.  You can find those brackets on any keyboard between the shift key and letter Z.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>:  Nice! Please, keep on telling me about the rules to work with HTML.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Well, HTML is not case sensitive. You can use lowercase or uppercase to write the same codes. I suggest choosing only one in order to have consistency. You must also learn to identify container and empty tags. Container tags wrap texts between an opening and a closing tag which needs to have a forward slash to tell the browser the tag ended. And, Empty tags can stand alone.", "image": "enpe8n3le03ob08re2img02.jpg", "time": "32000", "id": 1}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>:  Can you give me some examples of the different types of tags? <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>:  Sure. If you want the browser to display a horizontal line, you should write inside the angled brackets the letters hr. Now, a text between a tag that contains the word strong and another tag that contains a forward slash plus the word strong, makes the text bold. And the most common example of an empty tag is the line break, you just need to put the letters br inside the angle brackets.", "image": "enpe8n3le03ob08re2img03.jpg", "time": "81000", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe8n3le03ob08re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 1, "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Basic Concepts on HTML"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about HTML Basic concepts."}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Interpret the requirements report to determine the technological needs in managing information, based on rules and protocols established by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through the appropriate use of simple pronunciation aspects, and grammar and vocabulary structures.  Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic programming tools."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verb + Ing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When we want to use two verbs in the same sentence, we usually put the second verb in infinitive form (with to) or as a gerund (ending in -<span class=\"strong\">ing</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You usually add \u2013<span class=\"strong\">ing</span> to the <span class=\"strong\">second verb</span>  in a sentence after using some specific verbs. Take a look at the grammatical structure:<br /><br />  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + Main Verb + (<span class=\"strong\">Second Verb + Ing</span>) + Complement</div><br /><br />   Let's see the following chart:<br />"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Verb</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Suggest</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I suggest <span class=\\\"strong\\\">using</span> the correct tags. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Practice</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Practice  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">creating </span> your own web page.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Enjoy</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> She enjoys <span class=\\\"strong\\\">designing </span> websites. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Finish</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Let's finish  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">writing </span> the codes; then, we can see how the page looks. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Keep on</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We keep on <span class=\\\"strong\\\">learning </span>  about HTML.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I suggest choosing only one in order to have consistency."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Please, keep on telling me about the rules to work with HTML."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When you start creating a web page, you must use tags."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I really enjoying writing on those text-editors, they are very easy to use. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Hypertext"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">hypertext</span> is an electronic document where the reader can access other documents by using hyperlinks. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The prefix <span class=\"strong\">hyper</span> means over or beyond. You can find <span class=\"strong\">hypertext</span> in any computer display or electronic devices. These types of texts contain references called hyperlinks; by accessing a hyperlink the reader can see another electronic document, which may also have different hyperlinks to visit more documents. Tables, images, and other forms to present content that contain hyperlinks are also types of <span class=\"strong\">hypertext</span>."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "plain text "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "text without a graphical representation "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  You must write HTML in plain text and there is no need to use a fancy software to write codes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fancy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "sophisticated "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  You must write HTML in plain text and there is no need to use a fancy software to write codes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "forward slash "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an inclined line to separate letters and numbers (/) "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Container tags wrap texts between an opening and a closing tag which needs to have a forward slash to tell the browser the tag ended."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wrap "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cover something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Container tags wrap texts between an opening and a closing tag which needs to have a forward slash to tell the browser the tag ended. And, Empty tags can stand alone."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "keyboard "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a part of the computer with a set of keys that you can press to write"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can find those brackets on any keyboard between the shift key and letter Z."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le03ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Make a poster describing the basic concepts and rules about HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use a chart where you can write examples about tag, container and empty tags."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your work with your classmates and check pronunciation with your instructor"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about basic concepts on HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe basic concepts and some rules about HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give examples related to tag, container and empty tags."}]}]}